JA4 (TLS client fingerprint) — BSD 3-Clause License
===================================================

beacon is licensed under the AGPL-3.0 (see LICENSE). This file covers one
component of it.

`backend/internal/tlsfp` implements the JA4 TLS *client* fingerprint, and its
JA4_r, JA4_o and JA4_ro variants, from the published specification. JA4 is the
work of FoxIO, LLC and is released by them under the BSD 3-Clause License
reproduced below, separately from the rest of the JA4+ suite.

The remaining JA4+ algorithms — JA4S, JA4H, JA4L, JA4X, JA4SSH, JA4T and the
others — are published under the FoxIO License 1.1, which adds restrictions on
commercial use. AGPL-3.0 section 7 forbids adding further restrictions to a
covered work, so that licence is incompatible with this project and **none of
those algorithms are implemented here**. Do not add one.

The implementation is written from the specification against Go's
`crypto/tls.ClientHelloInfo`; no FoxIO source is copied or adapted.

JA3, from which JA4 descends, is the work of Salesforce, Inc. and is also
BSD 3-Clause licensed.

